    {
      "id": "Y3jegDnt_wNByJWdgpEyA",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1536.9662639047426,
      "y": 700.2229529418685,
      "width": 770.9084738017215,
      "height": 329.44499750619724,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b0j",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 526339248,
      "version": 9448,
      "versionNonce": 342398083,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1766342678820,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "1) For the searching of things based on the keyword that is in text format\nwe can use something called inverted index. In inverted index we store the\nmapping of keyword vs the list of references/ documents where that keyword\nis there.\n\n2) For the part where we are breaking down the content into keywords for\ninverted index its known as tokenisation. we use an ingestion service.\n\n3) Some observations about searching query. Here if a given keyword has\nmillion mappings then with the current implementation we will be returning back\n1M query results which is not a very good solution. One solution is to\nmaintain two different sort order. One based on the like count and the other\nbased on the time.",
      "fontSize": 20.273538308073675,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "1) For the searching of things based on the keyword that is in text format we can use something called inverted index. In inverted index we store the mapping of keyword vs the list of references/ documents where that keyword is there.\n\n2) For the part where we are breaking down the content into keywords for inverted index its known as tokenisation. we use an ingestion service.\n\n3) Some observations about searching query. Here if a given keyword has million mappings then with the current implementation we will be returning back 1M query results which is not a very good solution. One solution is to maintain two different sort order. One based on the like count and the other based on the time.",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
