    {
      "id": "_ywwz_CtZIWSp99dU_mD4",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 739.0259215238715,
      "y": 429.71059650283894,
      "width": 722.897812590283,
      "height": 600,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "#eebefa",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b6o",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1423259250,
      "version": 2982,
      "versionNonce": 845203395,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1766342709228,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "2) Non Functional Requirements (SPARCS):  \n- Scalability: handling huge number of users.\n- Latency: (<500ms) in terms of the search results.\n- high throughput in terms of the write.\n- CAP theorem: Availability >> consistency(eventual consistency)\n\n3) BOE Calculations\n- for this given problem What we need to know in order to make informed\ndesign decisions is a few parameters: how much data are we storing, how\noften are we writing to the system, and how frequently are we reading\nfrom it?\n- assuming we have 1B DAU\n- 1 post & 10 Likes per user daily\n- assuming 100k seconds in a day for ease of calculation\n- Post created = 10^9*1/10^5 => 10k posts/second. \n- Likes created = 100k/second\n- Searches: 1B/10^5 = 10k searches/sec\n- conclusion: we understood that this is a write heavy system.\n\n4) Core Entities \n- User  \n- Post  \n- Like\n",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "2) Non Functional Requirements (SPARCS):  \n- Scalability: handling huge number of users.\n- Latency: (<500ms) in terms of the search results.\n- high throughput in terms of the write.\n- CAP theorem: Availability >> consistency(eventual consistency)\n\n3) BOE Calculations\n- for this given problem What we need to know in order to make informed design decisions is a few parameters: how much data are we storing, how often are we writing to the system, and how frequently are we reading from it?\n- assuming we have 1B DAU\n- 1 post & 10 Likes per user daily\n- assuming 100k seconds in a day for ease of calculation\n- Post created = 10^9*1/10^5 => 10k posts/second. \n- Likes created = 100k/second\n- Searches: 1B/10^5 = 10k searches/sec\n- conclusion: we understood that this is a write heavy system.\n\n4) Core Entities \n- User  \n- Post  \n- Like\n",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "A2P4AILlBEj0BXizHjARR",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 739.6131573938732,
      "y": 1032.2950465970523,
      "width": 725.6259140844274,
      "height": 300,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "#eebefa",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b6q",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 408070254,
      "version": 2131,
      "versionNonce": 2146565805,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1766342718519,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "5) API Design \n\nPOST/post \n    Input: {content} Output: 2xx, success\n\nPOST/post/:postId/like\n\nGET/post?query=QUERY&sort_order = LIKES | TIME \n    Output: {Partial<Post[]>}\n\n\n",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "5) API Design \n\nPOST/post \n    Input: {content} Output: 2xx, success\n\nPOST/post/:postId/like\n\nGET/post?query=QUERY&sort_order = LIKES | TIME \n    Output: {Partial<Post[]>}\n\n\n",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
